            </note>
            <note corresp="#d346-f4" n="4" xml:id="d346-f4-content">
                <p>Another copy of this document indicates that telegrams 97 and 99 to Seoul were
                    attached. (Johnson Library, National Security File, Komer Files, Japan-Korea) Telegram 97 to Seoul, August 2, also
                    sent to Tokyo as telegram 331, outlined actions to be taken by Brown in Seoul as well as in Tokyo in order to
                    restart negotiations and help both sides accept interim agreements on several
                    issues to facilitate reaching a general agreement. Telegram 99, August 2,
                    forwarded the text of the oral message Brown was to give to Pak. (Both in National Archives and Records
                    Administration, RG 59, Central Files 1964–66, POL JAPAN–KOR S)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d346-f5" n="5" xml:id="d346-f5-content">
                <p>
                    Bundy wrote “Good. MGB” at the bottom of this
                    memorandum.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
